<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tur Ali Beg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tur Ali Beg was an early leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> tribes of the Bayandur clan, who pastured around Diyarbakır and the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> in the first half of the fourteenth century. He led raids on the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> in the 1340s, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutlu-beg">Qutlu Beg</a> later turned this hostility into an alliance through marriage to a Trebizond princess.</p></div>
